I walk over to a badminton court.
Three people are standing on the court.
"Hi, I am Kasper," a man says.
"And I am Sara," a woman says.
The third player is named Emil.
"I am Maya," I say.
"We usually play doubles," Kasper says.
"Do you want to play with us?" he asks.
"Yes, I would love to," I reply.
I really like to play badminton.
Kasper and I play against Sara and Emil.
We start to play immediately.
Sara starts the match.
The shuttlecock flies quickly back and forth.
Emil hits the shuttlecock high up in the air.
I love to smash.
I jump and smash it hard over the net.
It lands on their side of the court.
"Good shot, Maya!" Kasper shouts.
